Work:      Merlin Pro macro assembler -- distribution disks and catalog listings
Author:    Glen Bredon
Publisher: Roger Wagner Publishing, 1984-1985
Source:    https://archive.org/details/MerlinProMacroAssembler

The files here are three complete, unmodified Apple II disk images -- one DOS
3.3 volume and two ProDOS volumes -- plus the vendor's own catalog listing for
each. They are test fixtures for the disk filesystem layer, used because a
synthetic image can only agree with the reader that generated it. They are not
compiled into, linked into, or distributed with any Casso binary.

READ THIS PART. These images contain complete, runnable third-party software:
MERLIN.SYSTEM, PRODOS, BASIC.SYSTEM, the assembler itself, and more. That is a
larger thing to carry in a repository than source text, and it is here
deliberately rather than by extension of some other precedent.

Casso itself is MIT licensed. These files are not, and the difference is
per-directory rather than per-repository. Two obligations follow:

  NO DERIVATIVES. Do not alter these images, including by writing to one
  through a mounted drive. Tests MUST copy the bytes and mutate the copy. A
  fixture written to in place destroys the evidence for every later run.

  NON-COMMERCIAL. Anyone redistributing Casso commercially must remove this
  directory and the tests that consume it.

Provenance is verifiable rather than asserted: scripts/FetchMerlin.ps1 obtains
each file from the archive item above and verifies it against a pinned SHA-256,
which README.md also records.
